WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.449
Verification combines several jobs.

2
00:00:02.449 --> 00:00:04.688
Test programs exercise behavior.

3
00:00:04.688 --> 00:00:11.406
A testbench and a reference model help detect differences between expected and observed results.

4
00:00:11.406 --> 00:00:18.753
Coverage asks which planned scenarios or implementation structures were exercised, and which gaps remain.

5
00:00:18.753 --> 00:00:29.529
The CVA6 verification tree separates board support, simulation, tests and regression scripts, with configuration and simulator selections made explicitly.

6
00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:35.337
Architectural tests answer another bounded question about instruction set behavior.

7
00:00:35.337 --> 00:00:42.684
The ACT4 framework is useful here, but its own documentation calls for additional processor verification.

8
00:00:42.684 --> 00:00:47.442
This course does not claim that a particular CVA6 build passed ACT4.

9
00:00:47.442 --> 00:00:52.900
When reading a green result, open the run details and record exactly what ran.

